{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.A3BranchingModulusReflection","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3BranchingModulusReflection","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.A3BranchingModulusReflection.reduction_le_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3BranchingModulusReflection.reduction_le_one","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/A3BranchingModulusReflection.lean#L79-L88","doc":"**The reduction never exceeds `1` for a real branching (sorry-free)** — the amplitude form\nof `A3OffBlockDerivation.magnitudeFactor_le_one`: `factor_sa = 1 − x² ≤ 1`, so the self-adjoint\nbranching is a reduction. The lift `2 − factor_sa ≥ 1` is therefore the *reflected* value, and\nrequires the transverse leg `2x` — which the branching's own small `x` cannot make large\nenough (scope-(a), see the audit). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.A3BranchingModulusReflection.lift_sq_eq_reduction_sq_add_transverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3BranchingModulusReflection.lift_sq_eq_reduction_sq_add_transverse","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/A3BranchingModulusReflection.lean#L73-L77","doc":"**The lift is the modulus quadrature of the reduction and the transverse leg (sorry-free).**\n`lift² = reduction² + (2x)²` — the Pythagorean identity in the branching variables. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.A3BranchingModulusReflection.lift_eq_two_sub_reduction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3BranchingModulusReflection.lift_eq_two_sub_reduction","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/A3BranchingModulusReflection.lean#L66-L71","doc":"**Reflection about `1` (sorry-free).** The modulus lift is `2` minus the self-adjoint\nreduction: `lift = 2 − factor_sa`. The bar-odd unit-modulus reading reflects the branching\nreduction (`≤ 1`) into a lift (`≥ 1`) across `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.A3BranchingModulusReflection.pythagorean_triple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3BranchingModulusReflection.pythagorean_triple","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/A3BranchingModulusReflection.lean#L59-L64","doc":"**Pythagorean identity (sorry-free).** The reduction `1 − x²`, the transverse leg `2x`, and\nthe lift `1 + x²` form a Pythagorean triple. This is the concrete `A=3` bridge: the modulus of\nthe affine carrier `factor_sa − s·E` (with `E² = −1`, `s ↦ 2x`) is the hypotenuse of the leg\n`factor_sa` and the transverse leg `2x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.A3BranchingModulusReflection.lift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3BranchingModulusReflection.lift","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/A3BranchingModulusReflection.lean#L56-L57","doc":"The modulus **lift** `1 + x²` (the bar-odd unit-modulus quadrature reading). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.A3BranchingModulusReflection.reduction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3BranchingModulusReflection.reduction","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/A3BranchingModulusReflection.lean#L52-L54","doc":"The self-adjoint even-face **reduction** `factor_sa = 1 − x²` (amplitude form of\n`A3OffBlockDerivation.magnitudeFactor_eq`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.A3BranchingModulusReflection.asymmetry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.A3BranchingModulusReflection.asymmetry","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/A3BranchingModulusReflection.lean#L48-L50","doc":"The branching asymmetry `x = (a−b)/(a+b)` (the single scale-free datum of the\n`(3)↔(1,1,1)` bar-swap; `a = m₍₃₎`, `b = m₍₁,₁,₁₎`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}